---
import { runFor, shownSeconds } from "../../../lib/benchmarks";
import Speed from "../speed.astro";

// Biome against the ESLint toolchain; Oxlint is compared on /providers.
const small = runFor(42);
const large = runFor(420);
const speedup = Math.round(large.ms.eslint / large.ms.biome);

// Differences of the rounded times shown, so the figures add up on the page.
const biomeGrowth = Math.round(large.ms.biome) - Math.round(small.ms.biome);

const eslintGrowth = (
  shownSeconds(large.ms.eslint) - shownSeconds(small.ms.eslint)
).toFixed(1);
---

<Speed
  highlight="biome"
  id="bi-speed"
  stats={[
    {
      label: "Faster than the ESLint toolchain on 420 files",
      value: `${speedup}×`,
    },
    {
      label: "Added on Biome going from 42 to 420 files",
      unit: "ms",
      value: `+${biomeGrowth}`,
    },
    {
      label: "Added on ESLint for the same growth",
      unit: "s",
      value: `+${eslintGrowth}`,
    },
  ]}
  title="Lint, format and sort in one process"
  toolchains={["biome", "eslint"]}
>
  On Biome, <code class="font-mono text-base">ultracite check</code> is one
  command that lints, checks formatting and checks sorting, spread across
  every core. The ESLint toolchain runs ESLint,
  Prettier and Stylelint one after another, in Node.
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-foreground" href="/providers"
      >How Oxlint compares</a
    >.
  </Fragment>
</Speed>
